{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_module_3_authorization", "label": "Module 3 \u2014 Authorization", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a71.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The second and third defense-in-depth layers on top of M1's RLS; differentiator is enforced minimum-necessary via ABAC where legacy hospice EHRs ship coarse RBAC and every nurse sees the whole census."}, {"id": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_authorization_resolution_pipeline", "label": "Authorization Resolution Pipeline (RLS \u2192 RBAC \u2192 ABAC)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deny by default \u2014 a missing ABAC binding on a PHI action is a bug, not an allow. Existence non-leak returns 404 where a 403 would reveal a resource the user should not know exists. Authorization scope is pushed into the WHERE clause, never fetch-then-filter."}, {"id": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_abac_predicate_registry", "label": "ABAC Named-Predicate Registry (not a generic rules engine)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Predicates are typed functions bound to actions in code and evaluated against server-controlled context; a generic rules engine is an explicit architecture \u00a725 anti-pattern. Cross-module predicates are boot-registered provider seams with deny-stub defaults so M3 never reads a non-dependency table."}, {"id": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_break_glass", "label": "Break-Glass Emergency Access (D1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.5 / \u00a711 D1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "4-hour time-box; co-sign not required for emergency but required for non-emergency, because emergency access must be instant while non-emergency gets the accountability of a second signer. Every access under glass is audited at critical severity."}, {"id": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_auditor_engagement", "label": "Auditor Engagement (time-bound, read-only, scoped)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.5 / \u00a711 D2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_required_seams", "label": "REQUIRED_SEAMS Registry (D8)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a711 D8 / M03-F12", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Centralizes the seam-binding contract so missing providers fail fast at boot rather than at first call, and gives survey readiness a queryable map of who-consumes-whose-seam. M1 owns the registry and gate; M3 owns the schema of a seam declaration and contributes entries at init, since M1 cannot import an M3-owned registry."}, {"id": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_mn_namespace_ownership", "label": "Module mN. Namespace Ownership (D9)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a711 D9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every module owns exactly its mN. prefix for outbox events, audit actions and alert payload types; cross-namespace emission is forbidden. Gives unambiguous provenance, grep-friendly debugging, and prevents namespace squatting. M1's event catalog and M4's action catalog enforce ownership at registration."}, {"id": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_permission_catalog", "label": "Permission Catalog (code-owned, per-module fragments, arch:permissions CI)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.3 / M03-F07", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_role_catalog_system_locked", "label": "Role Catalog with system_locked CoP Permission Floor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.4.1 / \u00a711 D3 D7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Platform templates are cloned per org at onboarding so tenants own their catalog and may rename/disable/extend; the CoP-required floor is protected by system_locked roles that the role editor refuses to edit below."}, {"id": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_effective_permission_cache", "label": "Effective-Permission Cache (event-driven invalidation + 60s TTL, D6)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a711 D6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Correctness first \u2014 no stale elevated access \u2014 with a bounded TTL backstop; invalidated on role grant/revoke and role-permission edits, with permissions.changed pushed to affected users (the one permitted direct Socket.IO emit)."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_01_foundation_spec_v0_4_seam_registry", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_required_seams", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "M03-F12 \u2014 M1 owns the REQUIRED_SEAMS registry + gate; M3 owns the schema of a seam declaration", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_02_identity_spec_v0_4_step_up_policy", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_abac_predicate_registry", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "M03-F01 \u2014 step_up_recent predicate reads the M2-published session interface + resolveStepUpPolicy", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_02_identity_spec_v0_4_auditor_session_minter", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_auditor_engagement", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a711 D2 \u2014 M3 owns auditor_engagement; M2 exposes a boot-validated AuditorSessionMinter M3 calls", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_module_3_authorization", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_02_identity_spec_v0_4_module_2_identity", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "Depends on: 2 (Identity)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_module_3_authorization", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_authorization_resolution_pipeline", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_module_3_authorization", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_abac_predicate_registry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_module_3_authorization", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_break_glass", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.5", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_module_3_authorization", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_permission_catalog", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_module_3_authorization", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_role_catalog_system_locked", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a73.4.1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_module_3_authorization", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_effective_permission_cache", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a711 D6", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_authorization_resolution_pipeline", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_01_foundation_spec_v0_4_with_org_context", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a72.2 \u2014 handler runs query under withOrgContext; RLS enforces org boundary as backstop", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_abac_predicate_registry", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_05_patient_spec_v0_4_caseload_provider_seam", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a711 D4 \u2014 caseload_membership resolves through the CaseloadProvider seam", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_03_authorization_spec_v0_3_required_seams", "target": "docs_modules_wardenx_module_01_foundation_spec_v0_4_seam_registry", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/modules/WARDENX_MODULE_03_AUTHORIZATION_SPEC_v0_3.md", "source_location": "\u00a711 D8 \u2014 the M1 boot-time validateSeams() gate checks REQUIRED_SEAMS", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}